# Layout — bounded contexts

**When:** creating or moving Go packages, or deciding domain / store / handler / `cmd` placement.

Hamix backend packages live under `pkgs/`. Each **bounded context (BC)** owns `domain/`, `store/`, `handler/`, and `contract/` where it exposes HTTP or persistence seams. Live index: [docs/agent-map.md](../../../docs/agent-map.md). File-size limits: `CODE_STANDARDS.mdc`.

---

## Entry rules

- `cmd/*/main.go` — parse config, wire deps, start server (≤ 80 lines).
- `internal/` — not importable outside the binary; server assembly lives here.
- No `utils/` or `helpers/` packages — name packages by what they provide.
- `domain/` — stdlib only (no GORM, no HTTP). New types go in each BC's `domain/` — there is no live `pkgs/tasks/domain/` (retired ADR-0060).
- `store/` — SQL/GORM + map to domain; translate errors to domain sentinels.
- `handler/` — HTTP + domain + `contract` interfaces; no DB drivers.
- One handler file per resource group; one store group per entity.

---

## Monorepo root (Go-relevant)

```
/
├── cmd/
│   ├── taskapi/main.go      # Wire deps, call run(). ≤ 80 lines.
│   └── dbcheck/main.go
├── internal/
│   ├── taskapi/             # HTTP server assembly, agent worker supervisor
│   ├── tasktestdb/          # SQLite test DB helpers
│   ├── envload/             # .env loading
│   └── handlertest/         # Shared HTTP test helpers
├── pkgs/                    # Importable domain packages (see BC table below)
├── scripts/check-go.sh      # Lint + test groups (CI parity)
└── go.mod
```

- `cmd/` — entrypoints only; no business logic.
- `internal/` — single-binary or cross-cutting packages not importable externally.
- `pkgs/` — BCs and shared kernels; no accidental HTTP in `domain/` or `store/`.

---

## Bounded contexts (current)

| Package | Owns | HTTP surface |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `pkgs/taskcore/` | Task CRUD, deps, gate, retry, stats, ready queue | `/tasks*` (via handler register) |
| `pkgs/taskcycles/` | Cycles, phases, stream, verdicts, commits | `/tasks/{id}/cycles*` |
| `pkgs/taskchecklist/` | Done criteria CRUD | `/tasks/{id}/checklist*` |
| `pkgs/taskevents/` | Task audit event thread | `/tasks/{id}/events*` |
| `pkgs/taskcompose/` | Drafts + templates | `/task-drafts*`, `/task-templates*` |
| `pkgs/projects/` | Projects + context graph | `/projects*` |
| `pkgs/gitinventory/` | Repos, worktrees, branches | `/git/*` |
| `pkgs/settings/` | App settings row | `/settings*` |
| `pkgs/runners/handler/` | Runner probe/schema | `/runners*` |
| `pkgs/repo/handler/` | Workspace search, diff | `/repo/*` |
| `pkgs/storekernel/` | Shared store helpers (errors, JSON, validators) | — |

### Composition shell — `pkgs/tasks/`

Not a single domain anymore. It **wires** BCs for `taskapi`. Persistence composition lives in **`internal/taskapi/composition`** (ADR-0079) — there is no `pkgs/tasks/store/` facade.

| Subtree | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `pkgs/tasks/handler/` | Route registration, SSE hub, bootstrap, writepolicy, readpolicy — delegates resource handlers to BC packages |
| `pkgs/tasks/wire/` | `HandlerAPI` — composed BC contracts for the HTTP edge |
| `pkgs/tasks/postgres/` | GORM open + AutoMigrate orchestration (BC `store/model` lists) |
| `pkgs/tasks/realtime/` | SSE wire types, coalesce, `Publisher` |
| `pkgs/tasks/scheduling/` | Worker readiness predicates |
| `pkgs/tasks/middleware/` | HTTP middleware stack |
| `pkgs/tasks/handlerhttp/` | Shared HTTP JSON / path / limit helpers |
| `pkgs/tasks/apijson/`, `calltrace/`, `logctx/` | JSON errors and observability kernels |
| `pkgs/tasks/service/` | HTTP-agnostic bootstrap/git/retry helpers |

**Agents:** `pkgs/agents/` (harness, worker, runner adapters) — orchestration, not task HTTP.

